{"id": 10, "ts": 1784268111.2470682, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I acknowledge Agent\u202f1\u2019s strong case for Candidate\u202fC based on technical competence and leadership. However, the note that Candidate\u202fC is unfriendly raises a serious concern for crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014critical for long\u2011distance flights where cockpit harmony is essential. Moreover, while Candidate\u202fC\u2019s health habit of eating unhealthily could affect long\u2011haul stamina and responsibility, we lack concrete evidence on how it impacts performance.\nThe additional input on Candidate\u202fB shows he makes nasty remarks about colleagues, indicating poor crew cooperation despite his conscientiousness and stress resilience. This suggests that even strong technical traits can be offset by detrimental interpersonal behavior.\nGiven these mixed signals, I am not yet convinced that Candidate\u202fC outweighs the interpersonal risks, nor that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strengths compensate for his teamwork deficits. We still need to evaluate Candidate\u202fA\u2019s reliability and communication style, and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s moodiness and loner reputation, before finalizing a recommendation.\nThus, I propose we continue gathering evidence on the remaining candidates\u2014especially on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s operational reliability and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew cooperation\u2014before confirming any lead."}
